WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.853
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 4: Making Things.

2
00:00:03.933 --> 00:00:09.360
In this unit you will learn the
words for shapes, colours and clothes.

3
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:15.811
You will make things from paper shapes —
a paper quilt, a picture, a shape animal.

4
00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:22.419
You will talk about what people are wearing,
and dress up in pretend party costumes.

5
00:00:22.499 --> 00:00:26.746
You will meet the short 'e' sound in hen, pen and tent.

6
00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:31.624
Making things takes patience, and it is fun to try, try again.

7
00:00:31.704 --> 00:00:38.232
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:46.458
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
point to shapes (square, circle, triangle, rectangle).

9
00:00:46.538 --> 00:00:52.628
You will also name and point to colours
(red, blue, green, yellow, silver, gold…)

10
00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:58.569
You will also name some clothes and
costumes (hat, shirt, dress, clown, king…)

11
00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:01.388
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:01:01.468 --> 00:01:07.500
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
square, circle, triangle, rectangle, red, blue.

13
00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:12.824
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:12.904 --> 00:01:16.965
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:17.045 --> 00:01:21.822
The reading sequence includes Amal
Makes a Mat and Talk about Making Things.

16
00:01:21.902 --> 00:01:22.716
Read actively.

17
00:01:22.796 --> 00:01:27.126
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

18
00:01:27.206 --> 00:01:31.279
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

19
00:01:31.359 --> 00:01:35.208
The first language focus is Name your craft materials.

20
00:01:35.288 --> 00:01:37.754
Name one thing from your craft box.

21
00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:43.137
Say 'a' before most words, but 'an'
before a vowel sound: a box, an apron.

22
00:01:43.217 --> 00:01:51.067
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

23
00:01:51.147 --> 00:01:55.273
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

24
00:01:55.353 --> 00:01:59.894
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

25
00:01:59.974 --> 00:02:03.410
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

26
00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.065
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

27
00:02:07.145 --> 00:02:08.719
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:08.799 --> 00:02:15.839
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

29
00:02:15.919 --> 00:02:19.291
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

30
00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:27.274
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
